TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "August 2026" "hsh 1.0" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
hsh \- a simple UNIX command line interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a small UNIX command language interpreter (shell), similar to
.BR sh (1).
It reads commands either from a terminal (interactive mode) or from a
file/pipe given on its standard input (non\-interactive mode), and
executes them.
.PP
When started,
.B hsh
prints a prompt
.RB ( ($)\ )
and waits for a command line on interactive mode. No prompt is printed
when run non\-interactively (for example, when its input is a pipe or
a file).
.PP
Each line read is split into whitespace\-separated words. The first
word is the command to run, and any remaining words are passed to it
as arguments. Leading and trailing whitespace on the line is ignored.
.PP
.B hsh
then forks a child process and uses
.BR execve (2)
to run the requested program with the given arguments, waiting for it
to terminate before printing the prompt again.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B hsh
returns the exit status of the last command executed. If a command is
not found, an exit status of 127 is returned.
.SH EXAMPLES
Interactive mode:
.PP
.nf
.RS
$ ./hsh
($) /bin/ls
hsh main.c main.h
($) exit
$
.RE
.fi
.PP
Non\-interactive mode, with an argument passed to the command:
.PP
.nf
.RS
$ echo "/bin/ls /var" | ./hsh
backups
cache
lib
...
$
.RE
.fi
